      "title": "Oscillations as Control",
      "gist": "Brain waves actively organize and route spiking, and their electric fields act on neurons directly and almost instantly, making them good candidates for top-down control.",
      "question": "Oscillations — why are brain waves suited to control spiking?"
    },
